From 55b618fcd7092e12f586a3c4cd89e32305c105d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 11:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Foresight: content-driven tray sizing and polygonal layout

Trays are now sized and shaped by what goes in them, instead of being
hand-placed rectangles.

Tray design rules (polygon_shape_library.py)
Encodes the rules as executable constraints: bans squares, rectangles and
regular polygons; requires no two side lengths to match and interior
angles not to be uniform; keeps triangles wide-based with a bulbous peak;
feathers the perimeter within 0.6-0.8px; supports sharp, rounded and
mixed corners on the same shape. Silhouettes are seeded per tray, so two
trays of the same type differ visually but each keeps its shape across
reloads.

Generation is deliberately plump. An earlier gaunt sweep produced spiky
silhouettes whose usable rectangle collapsed to ~28% of the bounding box
versus ~60% for a plump one, which forced trays to inflate to hold their
content. Angular variance scales with vertex count, since a heptagon has
21 side-pairs to keep distinct against a pentagon's 10.

Content-driven fitting (tray_requirements.py)
Modules declare the space they need and never the shape they want; every
allowed family competes and the ones that cannot hold the content at a
sane size lose. Usable area is measured by inscribed rectangle, not
bounding box, because chamfers eat into it. Fitting asks only whether the
required block fits rather than computing the largest possible rectangle,
which took the full pass from timing out past 240s to well under a second.
Raises rather than shipping a tray its content overflows.

Layout (polygon_layer.html)
Renders silhouettes as feathered SVG, places content in the exact
rectangle the fitter verified, and lays trays out on the counter without
collisions - scaling the set to the viewport and seating the largest
trays first. Verified 8/8 placed, 0 overlapping pairs, 0 off-screen.
Deliberately not a grid. Also restores the tray show/hide launcher that
renderMenu() had left as an empty stub.

Content scrolls rather than clips: a status list or chat transcript
legitimately exceeds its visible box, and hiding the overflow lost it
silently. Requirements guarantee the visible minimum, not the total.

Also corrects the status panel requirement, which was guessed at 240x170
and measured at 570px tall for that width.

Tests: 31 passing (23 shape rules, 8 existing polygonal suite).

Note: foresight_ui_v18.html must be served over http - it fetches
tray_silhouettes.json, which file:// blocks. See RUN_FORESIGHT.txt.

